Core Model Pipeline

QuantGrad deliberately uses three specialised models instead of relying on one unexplained prediction.

Model
Main Input
Research Role
TrendModel
PCA-reduced time-series sequences
Estimates broader directional conditions and market regime.
StructureModel
Local market-pattern features
Identifies nearby structural context, such as momentum and price-behaviour conditions.
EntryModel
Raw feature windows
Assesses the timing quality of a potential research entry.
Decision Fusion
Outputs from all three models
Combines the evidence into a readable decision state in the frontend ledger.




This decomposition improves interpretability: trend identifies the broader environment, structure describes local context, and entry timing evaluates whether the current moment aligns with the preceding evidence.

