Troubleshooting

Issue
What to Check
run_frontend.bat is not recognised
Confirm that PowerShell is in the QuantGrad_V5_Complete folder, not its parent extraction folder.
Dashboard says the model is offline
Start run_backend.bat, then visit http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/status.
Backend reports missing artifacts
Run train_quick.bat once, or restore the required contents of backend/artifacts/.
pnpm is not recognised
Use run_frontend.bat; it avoids a global pnpm/Corepack setup.
corepack enable gives EPERM
Do not use Corepack on that Windows installation. The supplied frontend launcher uses npx pnpm@10.4.1.
Public-data card shows unavailable
This can be a temporary upstream public-API limitation. The rest of the dashboard should remain available.
Keras Lambda deserialization warning
Ensure the complete artifact set and artifact_manifest.json are present. The backend verifies trusted hashes before loading the saved artifacts.




GitHub Repository Guidance

The repository may include the saved model artifacts if they are needed for a class demonstration. Before pushing, confirm that the repository does not include secrets or unnecessary dependency folders.

Plain Text


Never commit: .env, .venv/, node_modules/, __pycache__/
Optional: backend/artifacts/ (include only if you intentionally want to share the trained models )



If any individual model file is 100 MB or larger, GitHub will reject a normal push. Use Git LFS or release assets for such files.

